  "raw": {
    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Hvac-Refrigeration_R-1889": {
      "title": "HVAC/Refrigeration Master Mechanic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Description As a selective-admissions, comprehensive public university, Louisiana Tech is committed to quality in teaching, research, creative activity and scholarship, public service, and workforce/economic development.  Louisiana Tech maintains as its highest priority the education and development of its students in a challenging environment within a safe and supportive, diverse community of learners. Are you a master of your craft ready to oversee the high-stakes infrastructure of a Tier 1 research university? At Louisiana Tech University, we don’t just fix machines; we maintain the environment where the next generation of engineers, scientists, and leaders are forged. We are seeking an HVAC/Refrigeration Master Mechanic to serve as a technical linchpin within our Physical Plant Department. This is a high-level role responsible for the climate integrity and mechanical health of the entire campus—from classrooms and offices to student housing. You will be responsible for the maintenance and repair of an expansive inventory, including over 11 absorption chillers, 40 Freon chillers, and thousands of air-handling components. If you are looking for a role that combines hands-on technical mastery with supervisory oversight in a stable, mission-driven environment, this is your next career move. Join us in keeping Louisiana Tech University running at peak performance. Apply today to build a legacy in the heart of Ruston. Minimum Qualifications Three years of experience or training in the installation and/or maintenance of heating, ventilating, or air conditioning systems. EPA Section 608 Certification Job Specifications The official job specifications for this role, as defined by the State Civil Service, can be found here. Job Duties As an HVAC/Refrigeration Master Mechanic, you will: Large-Scale HVAC Management : Supervise and maintain over 11 absorption chillers (110–400 tons), centrifugals (100–200 tons), and 40 Freon chillers (100+ tons). Campus-Wide Operations : Manage heating and cooling systems for all campus buildings and apartments, including 500+ residential units. Specialized Refrigeration : Maintain industrial and commercial units like walk-in freezers, ice cream machines, pony chillers, and reach-in coolers. Mechanical Repairs : Perform expert-level repair and replacement of compressors, motors, pumps, bearings, seals, and gaskets. System Maintenance : Clean and service evaporator/condensate coils, tubes, and fan coil units (over 2,000 units on site). Electrical Troubleshooting : Diagnose electrical issues, check and adjust controls, and handle the installation of control wiring. Chemical Treatment : Adjust solution charges in absorption chillers and manage the addition of inhibitors and alcohol as required. Infrastructure Support : Repair water and drain leaks and handle piping, ductwork, and cooling tower maintenance. Administrative Oversight : Responsible for the procurement of parts and materials and providing supervision to the refrigeration shop. Heavy Equipment Service : Maintain large-scale air handlers, including over 400 blowers and their associated gearboxes, shafts, and couplings. Position-Specific Details Appointment Type: This position will be filled as a Probationary Appointment. Location: Louisiana Tech University Physical Plant-Ruston, LA Work Schedule: The typical work schedule for this position is Monday-Friday, 7:30am to 4pm. May be required to work some overtime, weekends, or holidays. Annual Salary:  $46,842 - $84,302 (Depends on Qualifications) Closing Date: October 16 , 2026 Benefits: Louisiana Tech offers outstanding perks and benefits to eligible employees that include a variety of health insurance plans and retirement options, paid time off for vacation and sick leave, paid holidays, substantially reduced-rate tuition for employees and their dependents, discounted memberships at the university’s sports and wellness center, professional development training, and promotional opportunities. In addition, market adjustment salary increases are awarded annually (pending funding availability) for eligible classified employees. No Civil Service test score is required in order to be considered for this vacancy.  * Information to support your eligibility for this job title must be included in the application (i.e., relevant, detailed experience/education).  Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completed education and experience sections on your application. Applications may be rejected if incomplete. Contact Information: Louisiana Tech University, Office of Human Resources P.O. Box 3173 Ruston, LA 71272 Phone: 318-257-2235 Fax: 318-257-2482 Louisiana Tech University is an AA/ADA/EEO employer. Louisiana Tech recruits, selects, employs and promotes without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information in its admission and recruitment of students, educational programs, and activities, or employment policies. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration."
    },
    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Assistant-Director-of-Facilities--Residential-Life_R-1893": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Facilities, Residential Life",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. The Assistant Director of Facilities provides leadership and oversight for the maintenance, custodial, renovation, and facilities of all university residential communities. This position is responsible for ensuring that halls are safe, well-maintained, clean and conducive to student success. The Assistant Director reports to the senior level Assistant Director and supervises facilities staff, manages work order systems, oversees preventative maintenance programs, coordinates improvement projects and collaborates with campus partners to support the residential experience. Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Direct the day-to-day maintenance and custodial operations for assigned residential facilities Ensure residential facilities meet health, safety, fire and accessibility standards Monitor building conditions and conduct regular facility inspections Coordinate emergency repairs and after-hours work and response procedures Implement preventative maintenance and regular custodial schedules Supervise maintenance and custodial civil service positions and conduct performance evaluations for civil service employees Recruit, hire, train, evaluate and develop facilities personnel while fostering a culture of excellent customer service and teamwork Manage the housing work order system and analyze trends to improve operational efficiency Monitor facilities operating budgets and obtain quotes and manage purchasing of supplies and materials in addition to contracted services Coordinate facility support for conferences and summer camps in addition to the opening and closing of residential facilities for student move in/move out periods Respond professionally and timely to student, parent and staff concerns regarding facility issues. Promote a customer-focused maintenance operation that supports student satisfaction. The Assistant Director of Facilities must possess exceptional communication and leadership skills as well as demonstrate an understanding of building maintenance and custodial work necessary for oversight of facility management. This person should be available to respond to emergencies 24 hours a day, have an earned bachelor’s degree and three years of applicable experience is preferred. Qualified candidates who possess both the personal and professional skills and the appropriate experience required for this position are encouraged to apply. The salary for the position is $50,000. The position will remain open until filled. Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
    },
    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Assitant-Professor-of-Nutrition-and-Dietetics_R-1888-1": {
      "title": "Assitant Professor of Nutrition and Dietetics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. The School of Biological Sciences at Louisiana Tech University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, tenure track faculty position in Nutrition and Dietetics. We welcome candidates in any area of nutrition and dietetics or closely related field. The Nutrition and Dietetics program in the School of Biological Sciences includes an ACEND-accredited undergraduate Didactic Program in Dietetics (DPD), a Graduate Certificate in Nutrition and Dietetics, a Master of Science in Nutrition and Dietetics, and a post-baccalaureate ACEND-accredited Dietetic Internship. The successful candidate will collaborate with faculty across all Nutrition and Dietetics programs. More information about the Nutrition and Dietetics programs can be found at: https://ans.latech.edu/biological-sciences/nutrition-and-dietetics-2/. The School of Biological Sciences offers undergraduate degrees in Biology, Environmental Science, Medical Laboratory Science, and Nutrition and Dietetics, as well as MS degrees in Biology, Molecular Sciences and Nanotechnology (MSNT), and Nutrition and Dietetics, and a PhD degree in MSNT. In total, the School enrolls approximately 650 undergraduate students and 25-35 graduate students. Position : Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Nutrition and Dietetics Location : Louisiana Tech University, Ruston, Louisiana Department : School of Biological Sciences Start Date : March 1, 2027 Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in nutrition and dietetics consistent with the candidate's expertise and departmental needs. Advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students in their academic and professional development. Maintain a program of scholarship appropriate for a tenure-track faculty appointment that engages students when appropriate. Participate in departmental, university, and professional service activities, including student recruitment, committee work, and outreach to the profession and community. Minimum Qualifications: A PhD from an accredited university in Nutrition, Dietetics, Food Science, Public Health or closely related field, with a minimum of 18 graduate course credits in Nutrition. Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) credential and eligible for licensure in the state of Louisiana. Preferred Qualifications Clinical, community, industry, or other professional practice experience as a Registered Dietitian Nutritionist. Experience with ACEND accreditation or other academic assessment processes. Experience with graduate education, including teaching, advising, mentoring, or program coordination. Demonstrated record of teaching and scholarly activity. Demonstrated commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and professional service. About Louisiana Tech University: Louisiana Tech University is a vibrant and inclusive community dedicated to excellence in education, research, and service. As an R2 research institution, Louisiana Tech is dedicated to providing quality education and hands-on and experiential learning that engages undergraduate and graduate students beyond the classroom. Located in Ruston, Louisiana, our campus is at the heart of this thriving college town. Our university fosters a collaborative learning environment that supports academic excellence for students and professional growth for faculty. Application Procedure Applicants should submit the following: Cover letter describing your qualifications and interest in the position, curriculum vitae, copies of unofficial transcripts, Commission on Dietetics Registration credential, statement of teaching philosophy, scholarly interests, and future plans, and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Jennifer Hanson at jhanson@latech.edu . Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
    },
    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Director---School-of-Aviation_R-1886": {
      "title": "Director,  School of Aviation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. Louisiana Tech University seeks applicants for the position of Director of the School of Aviation (SOA). The Director will provide leadership and oversight of daily academic activities and Part 141 flight training operations within the SOA. This 12-month, full-time faculty position reports directly to the Dean, College of Liberal Arts. The SOA is accredited by the Aviation Accreditation Board International (AABI). The Director will serve as administrative and fiscal officer of the School of Aviation and will represent the SOA and its programs to College, University, and professional constituents. The Director will coordinate instructional, curricular, developmental, research, and service initiatives of the SOA. The Director will provide guidance toward continued reaffirmation of accreditation by AABI and direction for the enhancement of the flight operations, facilities, equipment, employee training/recruitment, and safety practices. The Director will also strategically cultivate partnerships with the aviation industry and foster opportunities to develop resources and opportunities for the SOA.  As leader of SOA’s recruitment and admissions activities, the Director will preside over the selection of candidates admitted into the B.S. Professional Aviation and B.S. Aviation Management programs. The Director will serve as the primary liaison with students, families, and alumni, and as an ex-officio member of the School’s Industry Advisory Board. The Director will engage in teaching, research, outreach, and professional service activities commensurate with this administrative position. Required qualifications for this position include a Master's degree in Aviation or related field and a broad understanding of the aviation industry with demonstrated professional experience. Preferred qualifications include experience as full-time faculty with administrative experience in higher education and as a flight instructor/FAR Part 141. APPLICATION:  A successful candidate’s complete application package will consist of a letter of application describing how their professional history qualifies them for this position, current resume, contact information for three (3) current professional references who are familiar with the professional experience and qualifications of the candidate, and copies of all required certifications. Screening of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Background check required. Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
