    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Instructor-Director-Early-Childhood-Education-Center_R-1887": {
      "title": "Instructor/Director-Early Childhood Education Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. Louisiana Tech University invites applications for a 10-month, full-time position as Director of the Early Childhood Education Center (ECEC) and Instructor in the Human Development and Family Science (HDFS) program. The Early Childhood Education Center is a high-quality early learning environment serving children ages 3 and 4 and functions as a laboratory school that supports both child development and university instruction. The ECEC provides a model setting for developmentally appropriate practice, observation, and applied learning for undergraduate students through structured observations, practicum placements, and student employment opportunities. The Director provides vision, leadership, and daily oversight of the ECEC while advancing its role as a premier early childhood education center and an integral component of the HDFS curriculum. The position also includes teaching responsibilities within the Human Development and Family Science program, contributing to student learning, mentoring, and program development. The Director reports to the Director of the School of Human Ecology. Responsibilities include: Provide leadership and administration of the Early Childhood Education Center, including supervision of lead teachers and staff, program planning, and compliance with state licensing and quality standards. Maintain and enhance the ECEC’s role as a model early childhood program and laboratory school supporting student learning and engagement. Facilitate high-impact learning experiences for university students through observations, practicum placements, and student employment. Teach three undergraduate courses in Human Development and Family Science per academic year. Support recruitment, retention, and success of HDFS students. Collaborate with faculty to integrate the ECEC into academic programming and experiential learning opportunities. Engage with families, community partners, and university stakeholders to promote program excellence and visibility. Qualifications: Master’s degree in Human Development and Family Science, Early Childhood Education, Child Development or a closely related field required. Demonstrated experience in early childhood program administration or leadership. Experience teaching or mentoring college students preferred. Strong commitment to developmentally appropriate practice and experiential learning. Effective communication and organizational skills. For questions concerning this position, please contact: Dr. Matthew Thornton: mthornton@LaTech.edu . Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
    },
    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Financial-Aid-Counselor_R-1880": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. The Office of Financial Aid is seeking qualified applicants to fill a vacancy in the position of Financial Aid Counselor. The position is responsible for managing the TOPS state scholarship program to ensure that awards are credited to student accounts in a timely manner. This individual will be responsible for the following duties: Maintain a pro-active TOPS program to ensure there is a balance of funds across internal office systems and LOSFA and timely reporting of grades and billing. Award other grants and process student files, counseling students and families regarding scholarship requirements and financial aid regulations. Understand financial aid packaging concepts, correcting over-awards and processing requests for revisions on an as-needed basis. Help students and their families navigate financial aid processes and the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA). Financial Aid Counselors must display excellent customer service skills and have a strong commitment to quality service and professionalism. Each counselor must multi-task in an office environment with frequent interruptions and distractions while maintaining effective results. Efficient time management skills, compassion, empathy, discretion, independent work ethic as well as collaboration are also all necessary skills for this position. Louisiana Tech University provides over $100 million annually to its students through a combination of federal, state, institutional and private sources. The Office of Financial Aid operates under the Division of Student Advancement and works as a part of the University team to accomplish the mission and provide timely, accurate aid to applicants.  Required Qualifications :  This position requires a minimum of an earned bachelor’s degree in a relevant field. Other essential, required skills include the following: Hands-on experience with PC based information systems Proficiency with Microsoft Office products Solid written and verbal communication skills Decision-making skills with attention to details Work with integrity and confidentiality Travel as needed up to 10%. Preferred Qualifications : In addition to the above requirements, familiarity with the following would enhance an applicant’s fit for this position: PowerFAIDS software knowledge Understanding of LOSFA Scholarship programs and requirements Workday software or other Student Information System user experience Successful experience in a financial aid office.  Basis of Employment and Salary: Employment is on a 12-month basis. Employees serve at the pleasure of the President of the University. Relocation costs are not paid by the University. This is an on-site position. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of application. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.    Application Process: Applicants may submit materials online or via email or paper delivery to the addresses listed below. Application packets must contain ALL of the following: A cover letter outlining relevant experience in relation to its applicability to this position, A current resumé which includes a chronology of employment, The names, telephone numbers, addresses, and e-mail addresses of at least three professional references, one of whom was a supervisor within the last five years, AND An unofficial copy of your academic transcript from the school from which you received your highest degree. Incomplete applications will not receive consideration. Screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
    },
    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Director--Small-Unmanned-Aircraft-Systems--s-UAS--Program_R-1823": {
      "title": "Director, Small-Unmanned Aircraft Systems (s-UAS) Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. The Department of Professional Aviation at Louisiana Tech University in Ruston, Louisiana, is seeking qualified applicants for a full-time, twelve-month faculty within the College of Liberal Arts. The position manages the UAS ground and flight operation to applicable students enrolled at Louisiana Tech University. The s-UAS position requires: Preparation of schedules, maintenance records, and ensuring that course standards, training requirements, and objectives are met by each student in each UAS flight course. Maintaining prominent levels of knowledge and proficiency in the areas of aeronautics, UAS flight training procedures, and flight instruction skills. Accomplishing additional duties assigned by the respective supervisor. Coordinate research and scholarly activities with the ASSURE program . Responsible for ensuring s-UAS students are advised for and consistently perform the correct number of classes during the academic term. Ensuring satisfactory progress for each student throughout the training course. Routinely informing your direct supervisor of course progress. Responsible for timely course completion of each assigned s-UAS flight student(s), including completion of required paperwork and assignment of final course grade. Expeditiously informing department head of any scheduling, course, or comprehension issues that may impede or disrupt the student from successfully completing the training or completing the course within the designated time frame. Initiating end of course evaluation requests for assigned students. Recommending curriculum and course improvements when appropriate and developing new curriculum or course improvements as assigned. Responsible for accurately maintaining all appropriate records to include training, student logbooks, student signoffs, s-UAS checkouts, s-UAS tracking information, battery cycles, etc. Monitoring the maintenance condition of each s-UAS in operation and inform the appropriate persons of any s-UAS aircraft maintenance discrepancy issues immediately. Filing safety reports as necessary on any observed safety violations, or potential situations that may affect the safety of operations. Required Qualifications: 14 CFR Part 107, Remote Pilot certification More than three years of UAS piloting skills and experience, including familiarity with and ability to perform required flight maneuvers and procedures. Knowledge of and ability to apply effective instructional technique in the classroom and in flight. Knowledge of and ability to apply effective instructional technique whether throughout individual instruction or in collaboration with other instructors or in a team. Degree Requirements:  Master’s degree in aviation or bachelor’s degree with five or more years of s-UAS experience. Preferred Qualifications: Basic Ground Instructor (BGI) and/or Advanced Ground Instructor (AGI) certification(s). Master's in aviation related field and experience with collegiate aviation accreditation through the Aviation Accreditation Board International (AABI). Additionally, there are expectations that the individual filling this position will participate in departmental, college, and university committee structures where appropriate. The individual will also be required to help with academic advising of s-UAS students, assisting with planning, development, and revision of s-UAS flight and ground school curricula. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, engaging in research and scholarly work within the guidelines of the University and other duties as required by the Unit Head. Application: To apply, send a single PDF that includes cover letter, current curriculum vitae, s-UAS and any other flight time summaries, description of teaching experience and interests, and the names and contact information for at least three references. Louisiana Tech University is a member of the University of Louisiana System. Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
    },
    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Regional-Admissions-Recruiter_R-1870": {
      "title": "Regional Admissions Recruiter",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. Louisiana Tech University is seeking a candidate to   represent   and   recruit for   the university in the greater New Orleans area. This employee will work in the Office of Admissions as a regional employee living in   the greater   New Orleans, Louisiana as an extension of the university.   Manage recruitment activities within   the   greater New Orleans   recruitment   territory. This includes but is not limited to college fairs, private visits to high schools, presentations, and award ceremonies.     Follow-up recruiting with personal notes, phone calls, texts, emails, etc.   Plan and execute events within territory which include but are not limited to counselor breakfast(s), yield event(s), social(s), and counselor trips to campus.    Visit with   students and parents at determined meetings and locations or via online meeting technology.     Assist   with on-campus events as needed and attend annual, on-campus training.    Other duties as assigned.   Qualifications/Requirements   Bachelor's degree. Knowledge of word processing,   spreadsheet   and CRM software; interpersonal communication skills;   strong desire   to help students; knowledge of all   academics   areas; extracurricular activities and university policies and procedures. Requires residence or relocation to the greater New Orleans area, Louisiana (preferred residence in Orleans, Jefferson, or St. Tammany parishes).   Essential Functions   Ability to communicate both in writing and verbally; be a good listener and problem solver   Ability to assess past performance and brainstorm new and creative ways to meet goals   Requires driving a vehicle   Requires overnight travel, work nights and   some   weekends   Walking and standing 50% of the time   To Apply:         Send letter of application detailing why you feel that you would be a good fit for this position, resume, college transcripts, and three professional references through the application portal.     Questions:     For questions, please contact Colin Bailey, Assistant Director of Recruitment.    318-257-2752 or cbailey@latech.edu . Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities.     Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
