    "https://ulsltu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LATECHCareers/job/Ruston-La/Assistant-Professor-Nutrition-and-Dietetics_R-1867": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Nutrition and Dietetics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nFull time\n\nT hank you for your interest in employment with Louisiana Tech University. The School of Biological Sciences at Louisiana Tech University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, tenure track faculty position in Nutrition and Dietetics. We welcome candidates in any area of nutrition and dietetics or closely related field. The Nutrition and Dietetics program in the School of Biological Sciences includes an ACEND-accredited undergraduate Didactic Program in Dietetics (DPD), a Graduate Certificate in Nutrition and Dietetics, a Master of Science in Nutrition and Dietetics, and a post-baccalaureate ACEND-accredited Dietetic Internship. The successful candidate will serve as the Nutrition and Dietetics graduate program coordinator while collaborating with faculty across all Nutrition and Dietetics programs. More information about the Nutrition and Dietetics programs can be found at: https://ans.latech.edu/biological-sciences/nutrition-and-dietetics-2/. The School of Biological Sciences offers undergraduate degrees in Biology, Environmental Science, Medical Laboratory Science, and Nutrition and Dietetics as well as MS degrees in Biology, Molecular Sciences and Nanotechnology (MSNT), and Nutrition and Dietetics, and a PhD degree in MSNT. In total, the School enrolls approximately 650 undergraduate students and 25-35 graduate students. Position : Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences Location : Louisiana Tech University, Ruston, Louisiana Department : School of Biological Sciences Start Date : September 1, 2027 Responsibilities: Serve as the nutrition and dietetics graduate program coordinator, including graduate recruitment, advising, assessment, curriculum development, and continuous program improvement. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in nutrition and dietetics consistent with the candidate's expertise and departmental needs. Advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students in their academic and professional development. Maintain a program of scholarship appropriate for a tenure-track faculty appointment that engages students when appropriate. Participate in departmental, university, and professional service activities, including student recruitment, committee work, and outreach to the profession and community. Minimum Qualifications: A PhD from an accredited university in Nutrition, Dietetics, Food Science, Public Health or closely related field, with a minimum of 18 graduate course credits in Nutrition. Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) credential and eligible for licensure in the state of Louisiana. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical, community, industry, or other professional practice experience as a Registered Dietitian Nutritionist. Experience with ACEND accreditation or other academic assessment processes. Experience with graduate education, including teaching, advising, mentoring, or program coordination. Demonstrated record of teaching and scholarly activity. Demonstrated commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and professional service. About Louisiana Tech University: Louisiana Tech University is a vibrant and inclusive community dedicated to excellence in education, research, and service. As an R2 research institution, Louisiana Tech is dedicated to providing quality education and hands-on and experiential learning that engages undergraduate and graduate students beyond the classroom. Located in Ruston, Louisiana, our campus is at the heart of this thriving college town. Our university fosters a collaborative learning environment that supports academic excellence for students and professional growth for faculty. Application Procedure Applicants should submit the following: Cover letter describing your qualifications and interest in the position, curriculum vitae, copies of unofficial transcripts, Commission on Dietetics Registration credential, statement of teaching philosophy, scholarly interests, and future plans, and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Jennifer Hanson at jhanson@latech.edu   Louisiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity and ADA Employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment that values diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals, including veterans and persons with disabilities.   Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled. Please Note:  Applications must be completed by 11:59 p.m. on the Job Closing Date to ensure consideration. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the Louisiana Tech University may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks."
